  "caption": "Figure 4.V. Single-turn AFIM difference between the matched healthcare and arXiv prompt sets, before and after adjudication, with 15 prompts and 3 per level in each arm. The raw healthcare-minus-arXiv difference of +0.087 falls to +0.040 once refusal-then-redirect responses scored above the 0.1 band are corrected down to it. The left panel shows that the reduction is concentrated at Levels 4 and 5, where the adjudicated difference is 0.000, while the Level 1 difference of +0.200 is unchanged. None of the six Level 1 responses matched the refusal-then-redirect signature, because low-intent prompts elicited factual engagement rather than refusal, so the Level 1 difference is untouched by the correction and is the only cross-domain difference in the single-turn data not attributable to judge scoring. The signature matched 12 of 30 responses, of which 4 scored above the band and were corrected (3 healthcare, 1 arXiv); the remaining 8 were already within it. Wording, perceived severity and domain-specific safety salience are not controlled, so the residual Level 1 difference cannot be attributed to domain alone."
